event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":115,"item_id":"rs_049a850fa792c780016acd174c347c8194999e32e0a584ab75","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Planning SSR HTML forms**\n\nI’m thinking about implementing small server-side rendered (SSR) HTML forms that are accessible without needing JavaScript. The browser should be able to handle everything using just HTML and CSS. I'll need to ensure the server is capable of using forms with the specified API to use POST on the `/projects` endpoint with URL encoding for redirection. Also, I need to set the default SQLite path to `data/workboard.sqlite` and ensure the directory exists. Testing will involve spawning with a temporary SQLite instance for health and security measures, particularly focusing on invalid IDs."}

